; Whether each NRL rule's left context matches at a letter. letters's record for the letter (its place i, and its
; word with an edge, 28, on each side, padded to 15 cards, kept in cells 80-94) and then the letter's record of the
; left table (text/rules_left.cards) in: each rule's left context, its elements, then -2; then 0s, and -1. Out, for
; each rule, 1 if its context matches and 0 if not (a rule with no context matches). An element is four cards: the
; most letters it matches, the fewest, and the range of codes they can be. The left context is read leftwards from
; the letter before.
;
; Address Contents Label Opcode Operand Comment
  03            rec     INP   i        03-16: a letter's record
  04                    CLA   i80
  05                    STO   rd
  06            rd      DATA  0        (INP 80 + k)
  07                    CLA   rd
  08                    ADD   00
  09                    STO   rd
  10                    SUB   i95
  11                    TAC   rd
  12            new     CLA   i        12-15: a rule starts at the letter before, matching so far
  13                    STO   pos
  14                    CLA   00
  15                    STO   ok
  16            el      INP   most     16-48: an element; or -2, the rule's end, 0 nothing, -1 the record's end
  17                    CLA   most
  18                    SUB   00
  19                    TAC   low
  20                    INP   least
  21                    INP   lo
  22                    INP   hi
  23                    CLA   ok
  24                    SUB   00
  25                    TAC   el
  26                    CLA   z
  27                    STO   cnt
  28            wl      CLA   cnt
  29                    SUB   most
  30                    TAC   chk
  31                    JMP   done
  32            chk     CLA   c80
  33                    ADD   pos
  34                    STO   rw
  35            rw      DATA  0        (CLA 80 + pos)
  36                    STO   c
  37                    SUB   lo
  38                    TAC   done
  39                    CLA   hi
  40                    SUB   c
  41                    TAC   done
  42                    CLA   pos
  43            mv      SUB   00       (ADD 00 in right)
  44                    STO   pos
  45                    CLA   cnt
  46                    ADD   00
  47                    STO   cnt
  48                    JMP   wl
  49            done    CLA   cnt      49-60: too few; the rule's end
  50                    SUB   least
  51                    TAC   fail
  52                    JMP   el
  53            fail    CLA   z
  54                    STO   ok
  55                    JMP   el
  56            low     CLA   most
  57                    ADD   00
  58                    TAC   rend
  59                    SUB   00
  60                    TAC   rec
  61                    JMP   el
  62            rend    OUT   ok
  63                    JMP   new
  70            i       DATA  0
  71            pos     DATA  0
  72            ok      DATA  0
  73            most    DATA  0
  74            least   DATA  0
  75            lo      DATA  0
  76            hi      DATA  0
  77            cnt     DATA  0
  78            c       DATA  0
  79            z       DATA  0
  95            i80     INP   80
  96            i95     INP   95
  97            c80     CLA   80
